{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"type":"text","text":"This session is being continued from a previous conversation that ran out of context. The summary below covers the earlier portion of the conversation.\n\nSummary:\n1. Primary Request and Intent:\n   The user (cobbler orchestrator) has assigned Task #5400: implement srd057-mv requirements R4.1-R4.4 in the go-unix-utils project. This involves adding exit code handling and differential testing to the existing `cmd/mv` utility. Specifically:\n   - R4.1: Exit 0 when all files moved successfully\n   - R4.2: Exit 1 when any move operation fails (permission denied, source not found)\n   - R4.3: When moving multiple files and one fails, continue moving remaining files and exit 1\n   - R4.4: Comprehensive differential tests comparing Go binary vs GNU `gmv` reference binary\n   \n   The task explicitly states to modify (not rewrite) existing files cmd/mv/main.go and cmd/mv/mv_test.go, which already implement R1.1-R3.3.\n\n2. Key Technical Concepts:\n   - Differential testing pattern via `pkg/testutils.RunDiffTests`\n   - `testutils.DiffTest` struct with Name, Args, Stdin, Env, WorkDir, ExitCode, Normalize, ExpectedFiles fields\n   - `testutils.BuildBinary(t, \".\")` to compile the Go binary under test\n   - `exec.LookPath(\"gmv\")` with `t.Skip` for missing reference binary\n   - LC_ALL=C environment for deterministic comparison\n   - SIGPIPE handler via `sys.InstallSIGPIPEHandler()`\n   - SPDX copyright header required on all Go files\n   - 40-line function limit, 500-line file limit\n   - No git commands allowed (orchestrator manages git)\n   - Non-goals for mv: no --backup, --suffix, -u, or SELinux context\n\n3. Files and Code Sections:\n   - `docs/specs/software-requirements/srd057-mv.yaml`\n     - Contains the R4.1-R4.4 requirements (read via Explore agent)\n     - R4.1: Exit 0 on success\n     - R4.2: Exit 1 on any failure\n     - R4.3: Continue after failure, exit 1\n     - R4.4: Differential tes