{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_018cUmmsRm6aspx55s5KPDeH","type":"tool_result","content":"0\tid: srd057-mv\n1\ttitle: \"cmd/mv: Move or Rename Files\"\n2\t\n3\tproblem: |\n4\t  mv renames files within the same filesystem or copies and deletes across filesystems.\n5\t  The macOS BSD mv differs from GNU mv in cross-device fallback behavior and verbose\n6\t  output formatting. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n7\t  (gmv, installed by coreutils) on exit codes and observable file system state for all\n8\t  supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n9\t\n10\tgoals:\n11\t  - G1: Move or rename files and directories within and across filesystems.\n12\t  - G2: Support interactive, force, and no-clobber modes for destination conflict resolution.\n13\t  - G3: Support verbose output and target directory specification.\n14\t  - G4: Verify functional parity against gmv via differential testing.\n15\t\n16\trequirements:\n17\t  R1:\n18\t    title: Basic move and rename\n19\t    items:\n20\t      - R1.1:\n21\t          text: \"When given SOURCE DEST, must rename SOURCE to DEST if on the same filesystem, or copy and delete if on different filesystems.\"\n22\t      - R1.2:\n23\t          text: \"When given multiple SOURCE arguments and a DEST directory, must move each SOURCE into DEST.\"\n24\t      - R1.3:\n25\t          text: Must move directories without requiring a recursive flag (unlike cp).\n26\t      - R1.4:\n27\t          text: \"When DEST exists and is a directory, must move SOURCE into DEST as DEST/SOURCE.\"\n28\t\n29\t  R2:\n30\t    title: Overwrite control\n31\t    items:\n32\t      - R2.1:\n33\t          text: \"-i or --interactive must prompt before overwriting an existing destination file.\"\n34\t      - R2.2:\n35\t          text: \"-f or --force must not prompt before overwriting. When combined with -i, the last flag given takes precedence.\"\n36\t      - R2.3:\n37\t          text: \"-n or --no-clobber must not overwrite an existing destination file.\"\n38\t      - R2.4:\n39\t          text: \"When the destination cannot be overwritten due to permissions, must print an error to stderr.\"\n40\t\n41\t  R3:\n42\t    title: Output control and target directory\n43\t    items:\n44\t      - R3.1:\n45\t          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is moved, in the format 'SOURCE -> DEST' or 'renamed SOURCE -> DEST'.\"\n46\t      - R3.2:\n47\t          text: \"-t DIRECTORY or --target-directory=DIRECTORY must move all SOURCE arguments into DIRECTORY.\"\n48\t      - R3.3:\n49\t          text: \"-T or --no-target-directory must treat DEST as a normal file, not a directory.\"\n50\t\n51\t  R4:\n52\t    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n53\t    items:\n54\t      - R4.1:\n55\t          text: Must exit 0 when all files are moved successfully.\n56\t      - R4.2:\n57\t          text: Must exit 1 when any move operation fails (permission denied, source not found).\n58\t      - R4.3:\n59\t          text: \"When moving multiple files and one fails, must continue moving remaining files and exit 1.\"\n60\t      - R4.4:\n61\t          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file system state between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: single file rename, move into directory, multi-file move, -i interactive, -f force, -n no-clobber, -v verbose, -t target directory, directory move, and error cases.\"\n62\t\n63\tnon_goals:\n64\t  - cmd/mv does not implement --backup (make backups of existing destination files).\n65\t  - cmd/mv does not implement --suffix (override backup suffix).\n66\t  - cmd/mv does not implement -u (move only when source is newer).\n67\t  - cmd/mv does not implement SELinux context preservation (--context).\n68\t\n69\tacceptance_criteria:\n70\t  - id: AC1\n71\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv file1.txt file2.txt renames the file, matching gmv.\"\n72\t    traces:\n73\t      - R1.1\n74\t      - R1.2\n75\t      - R1.3\n76\t      - R1.4\n77\t  - id: AC2\n78\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv file1.txt dir/ moves file into directory, matching gmv.\"\n79\t    traces:\n80\t      - R1.1\n81\t      - R1.2\n82\t      - R1.3\n83\t      - R1.4\n84\t  - id: AC3\n85\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv -n existing.txt target.txt does not overwrite target, matching gmv.\"\n86\t    traces:\n87\t      - R2.3\n88\t      - R4.4\n89\t  - id: AC4\n90\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv -v file1.txt file2.txt prints the move operation, matching gmv.\"\n91\t    traces:\n92\t      - R3.1\n93\t      - R4.4\n94\t  - id: AC5\n95\t    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv nonexistent.txt target.txt exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gmv.\"\n96\t    traces:\n97\t      - R2.4\n98\t      - R4.1\n99\t      - R4.2\n100\t      - R4.3\n101\t      - R4.4\n102\t  - id: AC6\n103\t    criterion: \"Differential test against gmv passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n104\t    traces:\n105\t      - R4.4\n106\t  - id: AC7\n107\t    criterion: \"cmd/mv compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n108\t    traces:\n109\t      - R1.1\n110\t      - R1.2\n111\t      - R1.3\n112\t      - R1.4\n113\t      - R2.1\n114\t      - R2.2\n115\t      - R2.3\n116\t      - R2.4\n117\t      - R3.1\n118\t      - R3.2\n119\t      - R3.3\n120\t      - R4.1\n121\t      - R4.2\n122\t      - R4.3\n123\t      - R4.4\n124\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4a424b-a5c1-4a40-bc90-746ecb0643e8","uuid":"9940ffc7-a404-40b4-ba16-0f1383f455cd","timestamp":"2026-05-21T01:27:40.596Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text","file":{"filePath":"/private/var/folders/dl/cbns6zkx7txc7pt64b6cgzp40000gn/T/go-unix-utils-worktrees/5400/docs/specs/software-requirements/srd057-mv.yaml","content":"id: srd057-mv\ntitle: \"cmd/mv: Move or Rename Files\"\n\nproblem: |\n  mv renames files within the same filesystem or copies and deletes across filesystems.\n  The macOS BSD mv differs from GNU mv in cross-device fallback behavior and verbose\n  output formatting. The Go implementation must match the Homebrew GNU reference binary\n  (gmv, installed by coreutils) on exit codes and observable file system state for all\n  supported flag combinations, verified by differential testing via pkg/testutils.\n\ngoals:\n  - G1: Move or rename files and directories within and across filesystems.\n  - G2: Support interactive, force, and no-clobber modes for destination conflict resolution.\n  - G3: Support verbose output and target directory specification.\n  - G4: Verify functional parity against gmv via differential testing.\n\nrequirements:\n  R1:\n    title: Basic move and rename\n    items:\n      - R1.1:\n          text: \"When given SOURCE DEST, must rename SOURCE to DEST if on the same filesystem, or copy and delete if on different filesystems.\"\n      - R1.2:\n          text: \"When given multiple SOURCE arguments and a DEST directory, must move each SOURCE into DEST.\"\n      - R1.3:\n          text: Must move directories without requiring a recursive flag (unlike cp).\n      - R1.4:\n          text: \"When DEST exists and is a directory, must move SOURCE into DEST as DEST/SOURCE.\"\n\n  R2:\n    title: Overwrite control\n    items:\n      - R2.1:\n          text: \"-i or --interactive must prompt before overwriting an existing destination file.\"\n      - R2.2:\n          text: \"-f or --force must not prompt before overwriting. When combined with -i, the last flag given takes precedence.\"\n      - R2.3:\n          text: \"-n or --no-clobber must not overwrite an existing destination file.\"\n      - R2.4:\n          text: \"When the destination cannot be overwritten due to permissions, must print an error to stderr.\"\n\n  R3:\n    title: Output control and target directory\n    items:\n      - R3.1:\n          text: \"-v or --verbose must print the name of each file as it is moved, in the format 'SOURCE -> DEST' or 'renamed SOURCE -> DEST'.\"\n      - R3.2:\n          text: \"-t DIRECTORY or --target-directory=DIRECTORY must move all SOURCE arguments into DIRECTORY.\"\n      - R3.3:\n          text: \"-T or --no-target-directory must treat DEST as a normal file, not a directory.\"\n\n  R4:\n    title: Exit codes and differential testing\n    items:\n      - R4.1:\n          text: Must exit 0 when all files are moved successfully.\n      - R4.2:\n          text: Must exit 1 when any move operation fails (permission denied, source not found).\n      - R4.3:\n          text: \"When moving multiple files and one fails, must continue moving remaining files and exit 1.\"\n      - R4.4:\n          text: \"Differential tests must compare exit codes and resulting file system state between the Go binary and the reference binary via pkg/testutils. Tests must cover: single file rename, move into directory, multi-file move, -i interactive, -f force, -n no-clobber, -v verbose, -t target directory, directory move, and error cases.\"\n\nnon_goals:\n  - cmd/mv does not implement --backup (make backups of existing destination files).\n  - cmd/mv does not implement --suffix (override backup suffix).\n  - cmd/mv does not implement -u (move only when source is newer).\n  - cmd/mv does not implement SELinux context preservation (--context).\n\nacceptance_criteria:\n  - id: AC1\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv file1.txt file2.txt renames the file, matching gmv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC2\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv file1.txt dir/ moves file into directory, matching gmv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n  - id: AC3\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv -n existing.txt target.txt does not overwrite target, matching gmv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC4\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv -v file1.txt file2.txt prints the move operation, matching gmv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R3.1\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC5\n    criterion: \"go run ./cmd/mv nonexistent.txt target.txt exits 1 with error on stderr, matching gmv.\"\n    traces:\n      - R2.4\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC6\n    criterion: \"Differential test against gmv passes for all flag combinations listed in R4.4.\"\n    traces:\n      - R4.4\n  - id: AC7\n    criterion: \"cmd/mv compiles with no warnings under golangci-lint.\"\n    traces:\n      - R1.1\n      - R1.2\n      - R1.3\n      - R1.4\n      - R2.1\n      - R2.2\n      - R2.3\n      - R2.4\n      - R3.1\n      - R3.2\n      - R3.3\n      - R4.1\n      - R4.2\n      - R4.3\n      - R4.4\n","numLines":125,"startLine":0,"totalLines":125}}}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_019ZSD5EvzoCEL8VaEqDFjpk","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"thinking","thinking":"Now I have a clear picture of the existing code and what needs to be done:\n\n1. **R4.1 (Exit 0 on success)** - Already implemented. The `moveSingle` and `moveMultiple` functions return 0 on success, and `main` only calls `os.Exit` when code != 0.\n\n2. **R4.2 (Exit 1 on failure)** - Already implemented. Both `moveSingle` and `moveMultiple` return 1 on error, and `main` passes that through.\n\n\n3. **R4.3 (Continue after failure, exit 1)** - Already implemented. `moveMultiple` sets `code = 1` on error but continues the loop with `continue`.\n\n4. **R4.4 (Differential tests)** - The existing tests already cover many scenarios, but I need to add specific R4.x tests that explicitly verify exit codes and the \"continue after failure\" behavior.\n\nLooking at the existing code more carefully, `main.go` already handles exit codes correctly: it returns 0 on success, returns 1 on failure, and `moveMultiple` continues after individual failures. So the main work is adding differential tests to explicitly verify these exit code behaviors.\n\nThe existing test suite already covers many scenarios through `compareResults` which checks exit codes, but I should add explicit tests for success exit codes, failure cases like permission denied or missing sources, and multi-file moves where some succeed and others fail. Adding test cases... Looking at the implementation in main.go, the exit code behavior for R4.1-R4.3 is already correct, so I need to focus on adding comprehensive tests in mv_test.go. I'm planning to add explicit tests for successful exits, failure cases, and the critical partial failure scenario where some files move successfully while others fail but the operation continues.\n\nWriting test cases... Writing test cases...\n\nI'm realizing that for the partial failure test, when `missing.txt` doesn't exist but `good.txt` does, the move command should fail on the missing file but continue and successfully move `good.txt` to the destination directory. I need to verify that the implementation actually continues processing after encountering an error, which is how GNU mv behaves.\n\nGiven the test file is already approaching the 500-line limit, I should focus on adding just the essential test case for R4.3 that demonstrates partial failure continuing, since the other scenarios are already covered by existing tests. I need to update the package comment to reflect the new R4 requirements, then add a couple of targeted tests for R4.2 and R4.3 while staying under the 500-line limit. I'm planning to add an exit code test for missing files and a partial failure test that exercises the continue-on-error behavior. I'm realizing that `r1_1_source_not_found` already covers the source not found case, so `r4_2_exit_1_not_found` would be redundant. The key new test I need to add is `r4_3` for partial failure scenarios, along with maybe one more variant of that case. The main implementation in main.go already handles the required functionality, so I'll focus on just adding the `r4_3` test and updating the comments.","signature":""}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":12684,"cache_read_input_tokens":20635,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":12684},"output_tokens":8,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"4b4a424b-a5c1-4a40-bc90-746ecb0643e8","uuid":"02e537a4-b120-4676-90fd-70b812dfbef8"}
